; CoreIR sample, family: admission and refund (Alloc, Free, LimitEnter, LimitExit,
; growth `like`, a finalizer's grant). FORM v1a, MEM-19..29, N03.
;
; Source (package samples@0, module admission):
;   i0  fn twice(n: u64) -> (bool, u64)            ; two n-byte owners; the second's result
;       fn bound(b: u64, k: u64) -> (bool, u64, u64) { bound bytes b { Box.new(k bytes) } }
;       fn grow(x: u64) -> (u64, u64)              ; an owner made outside a bound grows inside
;       resource Big { k: u64 } grant 32 drop { Box.new(self.k bytes) }
;       fn finish(k: u64) { let b = Big { k } }
;
; A refused allocation is an error value, never a failure (FAIL-2): `alloc` yields a
; null pointer and the room left in the limit it tried (MEM-22 `available`); on
; success `available` is the room before the charge. `limit_enter b` admits b against
; the current limit and makes a limit of b current; `limit_exit` returns its unused
; part to the parent and forwards its record there, so live blocks made inside stay
; charged and are refunded to the parent later (MEM-20, MEM-25). Growth `like v`
; admits against the limit v was charged to, not the current one (MEM-26), except
; inside a finalizer, whose grant takes precedence (N03); there, a refusal is the
; failure `Capacity` in the resource's cell (MEM-27). Big is charged 72: storage 8,
; cell 32, grant 32.
; f1 probes the parent's room after the exit with a `limit_enter` of 2^64 - 1, which a
; finite limit refuses, so it is run under a limit. f2 and f3 elide refusal branches;
; every charge in their runs is admitted.
;
; Behaviour, derived by hand:
; run limit 100: f0(64) -> false, 36 | used 0         ; 64 admitted, 64 more refused
; run limit 100: f0(40) -> true, 60 | used 0
; run limit 100: f1(50, 40) -> true, 50, 60 | used 0  ; 40 stays charged, 10 handed back
; run limit 100: f1(30, 60) -> false, 30, 100 | used 0 ; refused by the bound's 30, not 70
; run limit 100: f1(200, 1) -> false, 100, 100 | used 0 ; the bound itself is refused
; run limit 100: f2(7) -> 7, 76 | used 0              ; root 8 + bound 16 used: room 76
; run: f3(16) -> | used 0                             ; the finalizer's 16 fits its 32
; run: f3(48) -> fail Capacity | used 32              ; 48 > 32 although the root has room
